course: dictionary
lesson: 4712
title: Hoof
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A hoof is the hard part at the end of an animal's foot. Horses, cows, deer, goats, sheep and pigs all have hooves. Read the context: «A horse has 4 legs, and each leg ends in a hoof, so a horse has 4 hooves.» The words "each leg ends in" tell you where a hoof is: at the bottom of the leg.
explain: Hooves is the plural of hoof, meaning more than one. The word changes when there is more than one, just as one leaf becomes many leaves. Hoofs is also allowed, but hooves is the more common form.
explain: Other sentences give clues too. «Water buffaloes pulled ploughs through wet rice fields in southern China for thousands of years; their wide hooves stop them sinking deep in mud.» Wide hooves spread the animal's weight, so it does not sink into the mud. A good check is to swap in your meaning and see if the sentence still makes sense.
fact: A hoof is the hard part at the end of the foot of animals like horses, cows, deer, goats, sheep and pigs.
fact: Hooves is the plural of hoof; hoofs is also allowed.
fact: Hooves are made of keratin, the same stuff as our fingernails.
fact: Cloven hooves are split in two, like a cow's.
fact: Animals with hooves are called hoofed animals or ungulates.
exercise: «A horse has 4 legs, and each leg ends in a hoof, so a horse has 4 hooves.» How many hooves does a horse have? | 6 | 1 | *4 | 2
exercise: «Water buffaloes pulled ploughs through wet rice fields in southern China for thousands of years; their wide hooves stop them sinking deep in mud.» What do the wide hooves help a buffalo do? | Run faster than a horse | Climb up trees | Dig for lichen in the snow | *Stop itself sinking deep in mud
exercise: A farrier works with animals every day. What does a farrier do? | Milks the cows each morning | Bakes bread for the farm | Catches fish in the river | *Trims horses' hooves and fits horseshoes
test: Reindeer have «broad hooves for snow and ice.» What does broad mean here? | Soft and warm | Thin and sharp | *Wide | Hard and shiny
test: Which word from this lesson means split in two, like a cow's hoof? | *Cloven | Keratin | Ungulate | Farrier
exam: «Cloven hooves» means hooves that are | Soft like rubber | *Split in two, like a cow's | Hard and round like a ball | Made of wood
